Runtime ClientConfig mutability (2026-10-08 21:07 UTC): pinned Java 5.5.1 `MQClientManager.getOrCreateMQClientInstance` clones caller input; `MQClientInstance` retains that clone and `getClientConfig()` returns the same mutable object. Added actual getter-identity and post-getter-mutation outcomes to the Java `RuntimeConfigFixtures` oracle and regenerated `client-config.json` (SHA-256 `ad49c9b917811d1b542bf7f8b2af9ffa07ba3cde22105a00a69bd02f2ade093a`). Oracle commit `96c51e4`.

Rust `ClientRuntime::config()` now returns `SharedClientConfig` (`Arc<RwLock<ClientConfig>>`) and the runtime-created API and namespace hook share it. Live reads cover heartbeat language, namespaceV2 request fields, RPC timeout, VIP address selection, heartbeat V2, and concurrent-heartbeat enablement. Constructor/start boundaries remain source-timed: transport and listener construction, stream hook registration, concurrent executor presence/width, and schedules at runtime start. The config input passed to `ClientRuntimeManager` remains isolated from mutation through the returned runtime handle. Native tests cover getter mutability, source input isolation, heartbeat API/hook fields, timeout, post-construction VIP and V2 settings, and captured concurrent width. Implementation commit `ac01ec0`.

Updated ADR-0001 to distinguish the lower-level remoting transport snapshot from core runtime config; added ADR-0037; refreshed the Phase 6 API/config, runtime, requirement, and Java compatibility records; clarified the Phase 3 accepted difference; no plan files were edited.

Validation: `cargo test --workspace --all-targets --locked` passed with loopback access; strict `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` passed; pinned offline `mvn -o -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` completed BUILD SUCCESS with fixture replay and manifest22; comparator self-test passed; manifest validation checked 22 scenarios; `cargo fmt --all --check` and `git diff --check` passed. The first sandboxed loopback run was denied socket access; the authorized loopback rerun passed. No Broker was contacted. P6-V01/V02/V03/U01 remain UNIT_VERIFIED; P6-V04 remains PENDING_PHASE_19. Full Phase 6 bidirectional source/API/field/branch and final plan/index reconciliation remain open; Phase 6 is still partial.


Follow-up after the full run: added `enabling_concurrent_heartbeat_after_construction_has_no_executor` to prove the pinned Java boundary when the live enable flag is turned on after construction did not create an executor. The focused loopback test passed. Test-only commit `7e0992d`; strict all-target Clippy, formatting, diff, comparator, and manifest checks are rerun with the documentation commit.

Route DTO input boundary continuation (2026-10-08 21:17 UTC): extended `RuntimeRouteFixtures.routeDtoInputCases` from 25 to 37 actual Java inputs. Twelve new syntax/shape cases show that route `JSON.parseObject` rejects single quotes, comments, unquoted keys, trailing commas, `L`/`D`/`F` numeric suffixes, scalar filter-list values, array-shaped maps, scalar route rows, and null map values. These establish a strict route DTO parser boundary distinct from the separately audited permissive SOCKS constructor parser. Rust's native route DTO decoder rejects the same inputs. Fixture SHA-256 `6de3936438f326e57114da010a1363ae730c7a17de2913293472c7c91547c6bf`; Java oracle/native test commit `aa34861`.

Validation: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol route_dto_inputs_match_invoked_java_fastjson --locked` passed; `mvn -o -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` completed BUILD SUCCESS, including route/config/heartbeat replay and manifest22; `cargo fmt --all --check` and `git diff --check` passed. No production parser behavior changed. Updated ADR-0014, API map, requirement audit, runtime inventory, Java compatibility summary, and this append-only log. Wider DTO/input/source/field/branch reconciliation remains open; P6-V04 stays PENDING_PHASE_19.
